content:
Check the exclusions before drafting anything, and report what was skipped rather than staying silent about it.

Never chase:
- any customer, domain or invoice reference in the installation's 'never_chase' setting;
- an invoice with an open dispute, chargeback or credit note in flight;
- an invoice on an agreed payment plan that is being honoured;
- an invoice already paid by another route, even when Stripe still shows it open — check for a payment recorded against the reference first;
- an invoice whose customer replied since the last chase and is waiting on an answer from your side. Chasing someone who is waiting on you is the fastest way to lose the account.

Once an invoice has received the number of chases in the 'max_chases' setting, stop drafting for it. Say once, plainly, that it has stopped and what the last chase was; do not repeat that notice on later runs.
